Context()->texStrings;
BEGIN_TEXT
Let \( F(x,y,z) = \text{Curl} (x^5 - 2zy, z^3-2, 4x\sin(z)) \) and let \( S \) be the upper half of the ellipsoid \( x^2 + \dfrac{y^2}{9} + 4z^2 = 1 \) with upward normal. Compute the flux of \( F \) along \( S \) by moving the integral to another surface.

$BR
\{$q1->ans_rule\}

END_TEXT
Context()->normalStrings;

